From 05672c8cabaabd1f984f618721723e6a1527533b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@local>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:08:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/32] Direct3D layer on pbkit, step 1 (device bring-up);
 engine start-up without DLLs; fonts compile

- xbox/d3d8: Direct3DCreate8, device creation on pbkit (640x480, 32-bit color, D24S8),
  Clear as the NV2A's clear command, Present, frames that begin at Clear or BeginScene,
  viewport and stored render state, textures/surfaces/vertex and index buffers in GPU-visible
  memory, D3DX texture helpers (conversion and box-filtered mipmaps). Drawing is step 2.
- reported vendor is 'unidentified': the engine's NVIDIA workaround would disable DXT1
- DX8Wrapper: Direct3DCreate8 called directly (no D3D8.DLL), via a WINAPI wrapper
- animatedsoundmgr_xbox.cpp: placeholder until audio, same behaviour as with no sounds
- render2dsentence.cpp compiles: its three GDI functions have placeholders (empty glyphs at
  realistic sizes) until the SDL_ttf font replacement
---
